==== enter in the middle of a line moves the cursor to the start of the new line
abc
def
----
lia<CR>

==== enter then typing continues at the start of the new line
abc
def
----
li<CR>x<ESC>

==== enter in the middle of an indented line
  abc
def
----
llli<CR>

==== enter at the end of a line
abc
def
----
A<CR>x<ESC>

==== enter in the indent keeps the indent before the cursor
  abc
def
----
li<CR>x<ESC>

==== enter at the start of an indented line drops its indent
  abc
def
----
0i<CR>x<ESC>

==== enter before whitespace drops the whitespace
a  bc
def
----
li<CR>x<ESC>

==== enter after whitespace keeps it on the first line
  a bc
def
----
llli<CR>x<ESC>

==== O above an indented line keeps the line's indent
  abc
def
----
Ox<ESC>

==== o below an indented line indents the new line
  abc
def
----
ox<ESC>
